# Next.js Frontend Conventions

## Structure

- App Router: pages and layouts in `apps/web/app/`.
- Shared UI: Shadcn components in `apps/web/components/ui/`.
- App-specific components: `apps/web/app/components/`.
- API helpers and types: `apps/web/lib/`.

## Data fetching

- Use SWR (`swr`) for client-side API calls.
- API base URL from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (set to `http://localhost:3001` in Docker).
- Auth token passed via query param on OAuth redirect; store and attach to requests as established in existing code.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS with CSS variables defined in `globals.css`.
- Dark zinc theme with green primary — match existing tokens, do not introduce conflicting color systems.
- Use `cn()` from `lib/utils.ts` for conditional classes.

## Adding Shadcn components

Run inside the `web` container from `/app`:

```bash
docker compose exec web sh -c "cd apps/web && pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>"
```

## Do not

- Use Pages Router patterns (`pages/` directory).
- Bypass `components/ui/` for standard primitives (Button, Dialog, Input, etc.).
- Call the API with hardcoded URLs — always use env-based configuration.
